id=ecarx_e02_ihu717p_bt
name=IHU717P BLE/Classic Bluetooth support
version=2026.07.27.1
versionCode=20260728
author=Dmitry Nearlyny
description=Bluetooth support for ECARX E02 / IHU717P based Geely and Knewstar head units at the stock app path: A2DP Sink, HFP HF Client, PBAP Client, AVRCP Controller with working track metadata and physical media buttons (native libbluetooth.so AVRCP feature-negotiation fix), CarPlay/GOC watchdog. Force-connects A2DP Sink for phones that advertise A2DP but never offer a "Media audio" toggle (e.g. Samsung Galaxy) - without it those phones stay call-only. Disables MAP MCE (profile_supported_mapmce=false, patched directly in resources.arsc so classes.dex stays byte-identical to stock) - MAP made Android links refuse sniff during calls (hci_status=26), starving BLE/HWGPS, and has no use here (no message pop-ups). Fixes missing AVRCP track metadata on iOS: a GetCapabilities race (AVRCP comes up before A2DP, the request times out and AOSP never retries) left RegisterNotification unsent, so no track info ever arrived - patched in libbluetooth.so. NOTE: the stock NSMedia media app pauses Bluetooth unless the head-unit source is set to Bluetooth - select Bluetooth as the source (see README).
